  %% ---------- BUDGET ENGINE (DESIGN LOCKED — build next) ----------
  subgraph BUDGET["💰 BUDGET ENGINE — locked design (mirror the mood pipeline)"]
    B0["TEMPLATE EXISTS: mood/Just-Feed-Me already does library-first + AI-prewarm.<br/>callMoodChef → show DB page instantly + startMoodAIFetch() in background;<br/>getMoreMoodRecipes → DB pages first, then pre-generated AI bank. Mirror it for budget, keyed to (price, people)."]
    B1["1 · LIBRARY FIRST — exhaust ALL our recipes before AI. Instant local slice.<br/>Pool = priced MEALS (breakfast+lunch+supper) where costPP×people ≤ budget. (Sides/Basics + Bakes excluded.)"]
    B2["2 · FLOOR RECIPES — ✅ RECEIVED: 90-recipe budget PDF (9 bands R40–R120). Use ONLY as low-tier floor, blended with existing library. Higher tiers = library only.<br/>⚠️ PDF tier labels DON'T survive our prices (e.g. 'R50' Wors-Chakalaka = ~R72/4). Must RE-COST each with priceOf + assign tier by REAL cost.<br/>USE-CASE: the last few days before payday, money really tight — this frames the how-this-feels tone."]
    B3["3 · VARIETY JUGGLING — round-robin buckets so each batch of 3 is balanced: meat-flavoured · tinned fish · VEGETARIAN · SOUP/STEW · pasta/rice · beans/lentils. Blend the CHEAP LIBRARY we already have (vetkoek, mince dishes, etc.) alongside the floor recipes. Add more veg + soups/stews to the floor pool."]
    B4["4 · AI PRE-WARM — the moment a price (e.g. R50) is picked, startBudgetAIFetch(budget,people) fires in background. Keep a rolling buffer of ≥9 for that price FORMAT, topped up continuously, de-duped vs shown."]
    B5["5 · COSTED + PLANNED (critical) — re-cost EVERY AI recipe with OUR priceOf (never trust AI's number) + require structured {n,pp,u} ingredients. Discard if over budget once re-priced. This also fixes the old 'AI dish had no shopping list'."]
    B6["6 · SEAMLESS HANDOVER — library dry → AI bank already waiting → no pause. Re-key/cancel buffer when price or people changes."]
    B7["FLOOR — ✅ WIRED LIVE. sections/budget_floor.js = 9 recipes. MEAT-forward lead: Mince & Lentil Curry · Vetkoek & Curried Mince · Curried Pilchard Stew. Veg fallback: Samp · Soya-Cabbage · Lentil balls · Egg Curry · PB-Spinach · Double Bean. All ≤R15pp, re-costed. Blend into _budgetPool only when budget/4 ≤ R60."]
    B8["TIERING (clear now): FLOOR ≤R15pp = stretched mince / pilchards / beans / eggs / lentils — honest 'can\'t do meat tonight'. LOW TIER R20–45pp (R80–180/4) = proper MEAT meals (cottage pie, mince pasta, boerewors meatballs, samp & beef stew) from LIBRARY + cookbook gap-fillers. Meat naturally lives just above the floor — you can\'t always eat meat when broke."]
    B9["OFFAL (chicken necks/gizzards) → Tina: EXTREME cases only, not the go-to. Dropped from floor. Prices kept as parked data for a possible future 'extreme' sub-tier."]
    B10["FINDER COVERAGE (checked 2 Jul): _budgetPool pulls BREAKFAST + LIGHTLUNCH + SUPPER (+ FLOOR when ≤R60/4). ✅ SOUPS already show (they're Light-Lunch). ✅ VETKOEK now added to floor (previously only in Buffet/Events, invisible to finder). ❌ WORLD KITCHEN not pulled → see B11."]
    B12["♻️ AI RECIPE HARVEST / REVIEW LOOP (Tina, LATER): library-first ALWAYS; while the user browses, AI scouts in the background (budget prewarm + Just-Feed-Me). NEW: every AI-generated recipe is LOGGED BACK TO TINA for review → clean up · re-cost via priceOf · structure {n,pp,u} · name well · WOW → PROMOTE good ones into the permanent library. Virtuous loop: AI suggests → Tina curates → library grows → less AI dependence over time. Mechanics (later): capture in the Netlify claude fn (log/store) or a review queue view; new recipes then join the Universal Index. Applies to mood + budget alike."]
    B11["🌍 BIG OPPORTUNITY — WORLD KITCHEN into the finder. 136 SA dishes + African (bobotie, bredies, frikkadels, samp/pap dishes, pickled fish…) are NOT in the budget finder. BLOCKER: WK recipes have NO costPP and ingredients are stored as TEXT ('90g beef mince · 50g onion'), not {n,pp,u}. NEEDS a WK→budget converter: parse text ingredients (wkScaleLine/wkPriceLookup already exist) → per-person grams → priceOf → costPP; open via openRecipe('world') not recipeDetailFromResult; include only cheap MAINS (skip desserts/celebration dishes). On-brand (SA-first heritage). = PHASE 1 of the Universal Recipe Index (URI) below. Tina to greenlight."]
    B0-->B1-->B2-->B3-->B4-->B5-->B6-->B7-->B8-->B9-->B10-->B12-->B11
  end
