  %% ---------- UNIVERSAL RECIPE INDEX (make ALL recipes findable) ----------
  subgraph URI["🧭 UNIVERSAL RECIPE INDEX — make EVERY recipe findable (scoped 2 Jul, big roadmap)"]
    U0["GOAL (Tina): all recipes findable via one mechanism (budget = just the first filter). Reframe: the universal OPENER already exists (RECIPE_SOURCES/openRecipe for meals·world·health·events·cakes·beverages·spice·kiddies). What's MISSING = a universal INDEX: one registry returning EVERY recipe in ONE normalised shape."]
    U1["SURVEY — 3 buckets:<br/>• READY ({n,pp,u}+costPP): FMF ×5 · Budget Floor · Events · Health (the bulk — plug straight in).<br/>• NEEDS CONVERTER (text ingredients, no cost): World Kitchen SA(136)+Africa+Europe.<br/>• SPECIAL MODELS (decide include/exclude): Braai (portion-brain/calcMeat) · Beverages (drinks) · Tiny Tummies (baby per-age) · Spice (condiments)."]
    U2["WHAT IT TAKES:<br/>1 · ONE normalised record {id,section,name,emoji,diet,cuisine,time,kcal,costPP,ingredients,searchText}.<br/>2 · READ-ONLY adapter per section → normalised view (never rewrite a working section = low risk).<br/>3 · UNIFIED costing: every record resolves costPP via priceOf (doubles as app-wide pricing-hygiene audit).<br/>4 · allRecipes(filter): one index; every finder = a filter (budget=cost · search=text · dietary=diet · anchor=ingredient · mood=tag). Open already solved."]
    U3["PHASING:<br/>P1 = World Kitchen converter (hardest adapter → proves pattern + unlocks 136 SA dishes into budget finder). ← recommended start.<br/>P2 = wrap already-ready collections (FMF/floor/events/health) → near-free → universal SEARCH across everything.<br/>P3 = decide braai/beverages/tiny-tummies.<br/>P4 = finder UIs as filters (budget exists; add search/dietary/anchor)."]
    U4["PAYOFF: every dish findable by budget · ingredient · diet · mood · search, from ONE index; pricing gaps surface everywhere. Backbone of 'one card per dish, everything findable'."]
    U5["FACETED SEARCH (Tina): budget is ONE dial — ALL filters must STACK, e.g. 'diabetic + vegetarian + ≤R60 + freezable'. Mechanism: each facet = a field on the normalised record + a small filter fn; filters AND-compose over allRecipes(). Existing finders (budget · 4-ingredient · anchor · mood) become the first filters; every scenario is just another filter."]
    U6["FACET READINESS:<br/>• FREE: time (all have it) · ingredients (have/avoid; finders exist) · cost (ready collections).<br/>• DERIVABLE: diabetic/low-carb/high-protein/heart (from nutrition, 372 have macros) · freezable/fridge-life (54 freezes flags + 191 storage texts) · main-protein 'I've got chicken' (54 tagged + rest from ingredients).<br/>• NEEDS TAGGING PASS: diet (inconsistent: FMF diet:'meat/veg' vs WK diet:[] arrays — normalise + fill) · ALLERGENS (0 tags — derive from ingredient names) · kosher/halal (derive as ingredient exclusions)."]
    U7["⚠️ HONESTY CAVEATS (non-negotiable): Allergen / Kosher / Halal filters = GUIDANCE from ingredient names, NOT a guarantee (no cross-contamination / hidden-ingredient / certification visibility) → must show 'always check the label · not certified'. 'Diabetic-friendly' = nutrition heuristic, NOT medical advice → same caveat. Never let the app imply a safety/religious/medical guarantee it can't back."]
    U8["🍽️ MEAL COMPOSITION / PAIRING (Tina): cheap COMPONENTS in ANY section (Health muffin · Meals toast · a soup) become a full meal when PAIRED (muffin + side salad · toast + veg). For ALL users — 'older people on a budget' is just ONE persona among many, not the point. 'Cheap' is a FACET across the whole library, not a Budget-section feature.<br/>NEEDS: (a) mealRole facet main/side/component/snack — WK has course (66 main/27 side/…); FMF derive from cat (salads·soups·staples→side/component; stews·bakes·handhelds→main). (b) WIRE goesWith → real cross-links: 72 recipes carry goesWith TEXT but only 3 GOESWITH_LINKS hooks — wiring them is the unlock. (c) finder surfaces component + suggested cheap side as ONE costed meal — combined cost is FREE (2-item plan; two-cost renderer already sums plans). (d) AUDIENCE/persona facets — MANY (elderly · kids · gym/high-protein · single portions · quick-after-work …), each just another filter, none privileged."]
    U9["🎲 CREATIVE CONTEXTUAL SURFACING (Tina): the point isn't only findability — it's PLAYING with the whole library. The index+facets+pairings let us put the RIGHT dish in the RIGHT context, incl. unusual / cultural dishes (a 'strange' African dish surfaced when the scenario fits). One well-tagged library → endless contextual lenses (collections, 'tonight' picks, 'use what you have', persona menus). Everything we already have, recombined."]
    U0-->U1-->U2-->U3-->U4-->U5-->U6-->U7-->U8-->U9
  end


